&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;At LogicGate, we recognize that exceptional talent comes in all shapes and forms, and that there is no such thing as a &#39;perfect&#39; candidate. The qualifications below represent the core competencies, skills, and experiences that align most closely with the day-to-day responsibilities of this role - if you don&#39;t check every single box and are excited about this work, we still highly encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Engineer is LogicGate&#39;s pre-sales technical expert. You&#39;ll run discovery sessions to understand what a prospect&#39;s risk program needs to accomplish, configure and deliver tailored Risk Cloud demonstrations, build proof-of-concept applications, and ensure every prospective customer has a clear and credible picture of how our platform addresses their specific GRC challenges. This role requires both product mastery and a genuine curiosity about how modern organizations manage risk and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to our Solutions Engineering Manager, joining a small, close-knit SE team where your work directly shapes how prospects experience the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Solutions Engineering team sets a high bar because our work matters. SEs are instrumental in every customer decision, serving as trusted technical advisors throughout the buying journey. We hire people who are collaborative, intellectually curious, and eager to raise the level of the team, and in return, they join an environment where they&#39;ll be challenged, supported, and surrounded by teammates who make them better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
